🐛 Describe the bug
I want to reproduce the code from the tutorial Registering Submodules and Traversing the Module Hierarchy.
The code is copied from the tutorial verbatim.
#include <torch/torch.h>

struct Net : torch::nn::Module {
    Net(int64_t N, int64_t M)
            : linear(register_module("linear", torch::nn::Linear(N, M))) {
        another_bias = register_parameter("b", torch::randn(M));
    }
    torch::Tensor forward(torch::Tensor input) {
        return linear(input) + another_bias;
    }
    torch::nn::Linear linear;
    torch::Tensor another_bias;
};

int main() {
    Net net(4, 5);
    for (const auto& p : net.parameters()) {
        std::cout << p << std::endl;
    }
}
While running, an error pops up:
Debug Assertion Failed!

Program: ...ers\11588\CLionProjects\TorchTest\cmake-build-debug\mnist.exe
File: C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft Visual Studio\2017\BuildTools\VC\Tools\MSVC\14.16.27023\include\vector
Line: 1742

Expression: vector subscript out of range

I'm pretty inexperienced with C++ and libtorch, and I reckon this is related to MSVC.
Versions
I'm using the latest libtorch (libtorch-win-shared-with-deps-2.0.1+cu118) and MSVC. CMake build passed.
